WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.830
A cannon stands still on wheels.

2
00:00:02.880 --> 00:00:05.420
The ball inside it is still too.

3
00:00:05.470 --> 00:00:07.150
The charge fires.

4
00:00:07.200 --> 00:00:10.240
The ball blasts out of
the barrel, forwards.

5
00:00:10.290 --> 00:00:13.590
And the cannon itself lurches
backwards, the other way,

6
00:00:13.640 --> 00:00:15.020
on its wheels.

7
00:00:15.070 --> 00:00:19.470
But the cannon rolls back far more
slowly than the ball flies out.

8
00:00:19.520 --> 00:00:21.480
Why does it move backwards at all?

9
00:00:21.530 --> 00:00:23.500
And why so slowly?

10
00:00:23.550 --> 00:00:28.360
In this mission, you'll meet momentum,
and follow it as two gliders collide and

11
00:00:28.410 --> 00:00:29.880
stick together.

12
00:00:29.930 --> 00:00:33.700
Then you'll put your own predictions
about collisions to the test.

13
00:00:33.750 --> 00:00:37.410
Your mission: explain why
the cannon rolls backwards,

14
00:00:37.460 --> 00:00:40.280
and why it moves more
slowly than the ball.
